 "narrative": "Compared to last report: Trade activity Light. Demand Good to Very Good all markets of hay.  Prices on all classes of hay remained unchanged this period.  The southern half of the state has been receiving welcomed rain showers.  According to the CSU Colorado Climate Center's Precipitation Map, SW Colorado has received anywhere from 2.5\"-15.6\" of rain in the last 30 days with the heaviest concentration stretching from Conejos County, moving northwest to San Miguel County.  Per AAA Fuel Prices website, the diesel fuel current average price across the state is $6.3131/gallon today, down 20 cents from last week, up 24 cents from last month, and up $2.69 from a year ago.  According to the U.S. Drought Monitor's High Plains Summary for November 3, 2026, widespread precipitation (0.5 to 2 inches, locally more) resulted in 1-category improvements to the western third Colorado along with parts of the Northern to Central Great Plains. Recent precipitation and the \"convergence of evidence\" supported discontinuing the D3 in most of the Nebraska Panhandle.  For Drought Classifications, 11.30% of the state falls in Extreme-Exceptional drought (D3-D4) categories, and 88.70% of the state falls into the Abnormally Dry-Severe Drought (D0-D2) categories.  The next available report will be Thursday, November 19, 2026.",
